==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|intrust}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|en|trust}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈtɹʌst/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-entrust.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌst|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[trust]] to the care of.
#: {{ux|en|Can I '''entrust''' you with a secret?}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''entrusted''' me his daughter.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''entrusts''' that task to her.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1920|volume=15|number=2|work={{w|Classical Philology (journal)|Classical Philology}}|title=Hittite an Indo-European Language?|author={{w|Carl Darling Buck|Carl D. Buck}} |page=185|doi=10.1086/360279|passage=The study of the main body of Hittite texts was '''intrusted'''{{sic}} to the Austrian scholar {{w|Bedřich Hrozný|Hrozny}}, who in 1915 published a preliminary account of his results{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2004 |title=Uncanny Networks: Dialogues with the Virtual Intelligentsia |author=Geert Lovink |page=1742|ISBN=0262621878|passage=The first step toward finding a way out of this place begins when we take a flamethrower to Newt Gingrich cum Alvin Toffler style laissez-faire futurism, which '''entrusts''' our collective fate to the tender mercies of the marketplace, or New Age cyberbole that would have us pin our hopes to a millennial blastoff.}}

